  "reason": "R6 directly identifies SRO as a variable worth investigating in a refractory HEA, while R5, R15, R17, and R20 establish that ordered B2/L21-like structures and their fractions can materially affect HEA behavior. Thus, the records point toward deliberately varying chemical order in a refractory alloy. However, none connects SRO to lattice thermal conductivity, reduced lattice-distortion scattering, high-conductivity percolation pathways, or changes in the high-frequency phonon density of states. They also do not identify HfTi/TiZr clustering or Monte Carlo-generated SRO in HfNbTaTiZr. Reconstructing the specific intervention-mechanism-outcome would therefore require a substantial new thermal-transport idea."
